#question(title: [Unusual examples])[
  Construct three functions $f$, $g$, and
  $h$.

  + $f$ has domain at least $(0, oo)$, is
    continuous, is always concave up, and
    satisfies
    $display(lim_(x -> oo) f(x) = - oo)$
  + $g$ has domain $RR$, is continuous, has a
    local minimum at $x = 0$, and has an
    inflection point also at $x = 0$.
  + $h$ has domain $RR$, is differentiable,
    is strictly increasing. In addition, $h'$
    is periodic with period $2$, and $h'$ is
    not constant.
]
